00:07:03,529 --> 00:07:09,529
The Search for Signs of Intelligent Life in the Universe is a
comedy, tv movie film directed by John Bailey.

2
00:14:07,058 --> 00:14:13,058
The filmed version of the one-woman stage show written by Jane Wagner and starring Lily
Tomlin, which won the Drama Desk Award for Unique Theatrical Experience.

3
00:21:10,588 --> 00:21:16,588
The film stays true to the original stage performance.

4
00:28:14,117 --> 00:28:20,117
For her efforts on film and stage, Tomlin received a Tony Award, and Funniest
Actress in a Motion Picture in the American Comedy Awards.

5
00:35:17,647 --> 00:35:23,647
Trudy the Bag Lady / Agnus Angst / Kate / Brandy / Tina / Chrissy / Lud /
Marie / Vince / Edie / Lynn / Marge, played by Lily Tomlin.

6
00:42:21,176 --> 00:42:27,176
The Search for Signs of Intelligent Life in the Universe (1985)
is a one-woman stage show written by Jane Wagner.

7
00:49:24,705 --> 00:49:30,705
The original Broadway production starred Lily Tomlin, won the Drama Desk Award for
Unique Theatrical Experience, and was turned into a film in 1991.

8
00:56:28,235 --> 00:56:34,235
The show, Tomlin's second Broadway billing as a solo performer, follows Tomlin as she performs
various characters or personae, all while wearing simple black pants and a white blouse.

9
01:03:31,764 --> 01:03:37,764
The show appears disparate at first, but becomes unified under the sensibility
of the opening "bag lady" persona as the performance progresses.

10
01:10:35,294 --> 01:10:41,294
The show is often praised or considered controversial for its feminist material, most
notably the compressed history of the feminist movement offered in Act 2.

11
01:17:38,823 --> 01:17:44,823
For her stage performance, Tomlin won a Tony, Drama
Desk, and Outer Critics' Circle awards.

12
01:24:42,352 --> 01:24:48,352
A film version was directed by John Bailey and edited by Sally
Menke, and stays true to the original stage performance.

13
01:31:45,882 --> 01:31:51,882
The film earned the Golden Space Needle Award at the
Seattle International Film Festival.

14
01:38:49,411 --> 01:38:55,411
For her efforts on the film, Tomlin received a Funniest Actress in a Motion
Picture American Comedy Awards, amongst other notable accolades.

15
01:45:52,941 --> 01:45:58,941
A restored version of the film, compiled from different prints, was shown at the 2024 RescueFest
at the Laemmle Monica Film Center in Santa Monica, California in December 2024.

16
01:52:56,470 --> 01:53:02,470
The tone is lighthearted.
